:- module(tiarh, [go/2]).
:- use_module(library(prelude)).

% The spec's worked example in §The role of `any`: the head
% occurrence of the polymorphic go(A, A) allocates a rigid T, so
% R : T, and `R is 1 + 1` writes an int into a T position. The store
% chose T when the matched constraint was told, so the rule is only
% correct at T = int, which nothing enforces — an error. Declaring
% go(int, int), or guarding the rule with integer(R), states that
% intent and checks.
:- chr_constraint go(A, A).

go(R, _) <=> R is 1 + 1.
